    gas_offer_margin_zonal_anchor_vintage: { cell: "K", ev: "KEEPER 2026-09-13 (nyiso-231). PROMOTED under the owner's standing formula (verbatim this session: \"Is this a recommended keeper candidate? If so plz promote. If structural integrity improves but gates regress that may still be a keeper..\") — and BOTH halves clear. Run 2026-09-13-nyiso231-anchor-span, bundle results/calibration/nyiso231_anchor_span: all FOUR registered years 2022-2025 in ONE --years invocation, ONE bundle, solved ON-PIN (highspy 1.14.0). DETERMINATION at the ISO tier (2023-2025, rule 30(c)): NOT-YET (grade 6/8, 2 fails) -> CALIBRATED with C3c the lone ledgered caveat; C1 13/14 -> 14/14 (free 10/10), closing the incumbent's open cell C1-2024 CC_REGULAR share_pp 3.05 -> 2.7 against a 3.0 band. EVERY CRITERION IN EVERY YEAR IMPROVES OR HOLDS WITH ONE EXCEPTION: C3a 2022 -16.6 -> -9.9 % (FAIL->PASS) / 2023 +2.5 -> +0.6 / 2024 +3.3 -> +1.1 / 2025 -8.9 -> -5.9; C3b 2022 0.249 -> 0.209, 2023 0.122 flat, 2025 0.169 -> 0.149, and THE ONE REGRESSION is C3b-2024 0.174 -> 0.176 against a 0.20 band; C3c 2022 4 -> 7 h and 2025 2 -> 4 h, the first movement this lane has produced ON the tail. ZERO free parameters (rule 21) — the attestation's check (4) proves it by averaging the resolver's per-year output over 2023-2025 back onto the registered GAS_OFFER_MARGIN_ANCHOR_BY_ZONE table to its 4 dp. NOT the rules 1/13 carve-out: zero band multipliers, phys_* keys, peak bands or shares move in any year (measured), authorized_price_tuning NONE. THE STRUCTURAL CASE FOR THE COMPOSITION, new this session and measured: Delta_anchor(zone, year) does NOT factorize — the Upstate_West / Capital_Hudson ratio runs 0.7356 / 0.2518 / 0.2778 / 0.2691 across 2022-2025 and the zone ORDERING flips between 2023 and 2024 — so neither the zone-only nor the year-only flag can reach the level. REPORTED AND NOT ABSORBED: the four-year bundle reads NOT-YET on 2022's C1 (+5.20 TWh, +3.9 pp) and C3b (0.209); not a regression, since the incumbent's own 2022 touchpoint read NOT-YET on THREE failures and this fails two of the same three, each by less. AND THE PREDICTION OVERSHOT: PRECOMMIT Addendum A predicted the C3a spread would collapse to ~2 pp and it lands at 11.0 pp (from 19.9) — the anchor explains roughly HALF the measured slope, so phase 0's disclosed collinearity caveat bites and the remaining half is the handed-forward object. PRIOR SCREEN (nyiso-230, 2026-09-13) STOPPED on G-CONF/G-PRED and nyiso-231 found the cause was a defect in the RECORD, not the mechanism: run_calibration_full._recorded_config's mirror resolved the anchors ~144 lines ABOVE the block that sets gas_hub_basis_overlay, so run_config.json recorded Capital_Hudson 7.0563 where the LP priced 8.4431. Settled at zero LP, repaired by fusing one shared resolver to _recorded_config's return, and CONFIRMED here: the span's 2022 leg reproduces nyiso-230's arm price to 0.0000 $/MWh while its recorded anchor moves 7.0563 -> 8.4431 — an unmoved LP beside a moved record. Evidence: docs/RESULT-nyiso231-the-mirror-and-the-2022-rescreen-2026-09-13.md, results/calibration/PRECOMMIT-nyiso231-mirror-repair-rescreen.md, docs/FINDING-nyiso231-the-keeper-is-off-pin-2026-09-13.md, the bundle's computed calibration_attestation.json." },
