    cc_nameplate_summer_derate: { cell: "K", ev: "nyiso-214 (2026-09-07, ZERO LP, rule 28(b) stamp): CELL UNCHANGED AT K. This mechanism is the OTHER half of a measured rule-19 [R-ONE-MECH] collision: it reads the EIA-860 nameplate-net_summer gap as ambient derate and removes it in Jun-Sep, while cc_duct_peaking reads THE SAME gap at 11 of the same plants (819.462 MW of peak band) as duct-firing capability priced at 2.25x base HR in all twelve months. Proved to be one pair at 57185 to 0.0 pp and 4e-5 (P4). Every material CC carries a multiplier < 1 -- INCLUDING both plants that receive no duct band (55405 at 0.9246, 56196 at 0.8464) -- so cc_duct_peaking_pct's docstring defense ('for non-duct plants that same gap is ambient derate, already modeled') is measured to hold for the unflagged plants and NOT to exclude the flagged ones, which take both readings. Nothing changed here; the successor is a membership decision handed to the owner on the cc_duct_peaking cell. docs/FINDING-nyiso214-duct-gap-double-reading-2026-09-07.md. || nyiso-115 (row added by the shared-field census; scripts/mechanism_matrix_gap_sweep.py shared leg + check_mechanism_matrix.py shared ratchet) || nyiso-212 (2026-09-07, ZERO LP): CELL UNCHANGED AT K, the mechanism is a measured input and stays -- but a CONSTRUCTION SEAM with cc_capacity_reconcile (mode cap) is now measured, not argued. The summer multiplier this mechanism applies in Jun-Sep is net_summer/nameplate (arrays.py ~L834), premised on fleet_to_bins having carried the plant at NAMEPLATE (campd_bins.py ~L2298-2323); a cc_capacity_reconcile cap row moves that capacity to the CAMPD p99.9 AFTER the rescale (~L2462), and the ratio is still applied to it. At Cricket Valley 57185 the statistical factor reads 0.965 off-summer and 0.747075 = 0.965 x (1016.1/1312.5) in summer, on a capacity already capped to 1,086.9: constructed summer capability 841.4 MW against the design's 1,016.1 and a measured summer p99.9 of 1,078; the plant's own meter exceeds the constructed ceiling in 1,906 summer hours (261.7 GWh) over 2023-2025. Class footprint: 470.2 MW of summer capability removed across NYISO's 12 cap plants (Athens 126.4, CPV 63.2, Saranac 28.4, ...), the opposite sign at the 3 raise plants. This is the whole of the nyiso-211 hand-forward object (A): T_stat carries the entire over-ceiling excess in all seven months (pre-registered decomposition, P1/P2 falsified, P3 fired). A construction repair -- the summer multiplier divided by the capacity it actually multiplies -- is the named successor and needs its own gated field, matrix row and rule-29 screen; nothing is armed here. docs/FINDING-nyiso212-cricket-valley-summer-seam-2026-09-07.md; _nyiso212_overceiling_decomposition.json; _nyiso212_summer_seam_census.json." },
