    ramp_envelopes: { cell: "K", ev: "nyiso-188 (2026-09-04, RE-DERIVED AND A/B-SOLVED, K unchanged; FINDING-nyiso188 §2.1 / §2.3): the committed artifact reproduces byte-identically from its committed invocation with the Astoria remap entries stripped; under the routing 55375's row 1,252 MW obs / 469 up / 622 dn splits into 55375 (626; 372 / 449) + 57664 (626; 416 / 454) and the (0, CC) class-fraction fallback moves 0.4907 / 0.5623 -> 0.5000 / 0.5904 with its 26 -> 27-plant pool — read by 14 fleet CC groups / 1,355 MW (Selkirk 596.6 MW and thirteen 11-86 MW cogens), whose summed envelopes loosen 665 -> 678 MW up / 762 -> 800 MW dn. Arm 1R (2026-09-04-nyiso-188-ramp, zero config fields): ENGAGED BUT INERT at the annual grain — 318 / 2,565 / 5,307 price hours differ (max |dP| $0.47 / $0.37 / $1.07), 7-8k plant-hours differ, largest per-plant annual |delta| 0.0005 TWh, every criterion identical to the keeper; Astoria's largest non-outage hourly move (141.6 MW) never approaches its 363 MW net envelope. Carried into the promoted keeper as representation (rule 14), not as a lever. || PRIOR EVIDENCE: nyiso-111 (own artifact + bound-against-the-bound pre-check + A/B, PROMOTED KEEPER — FINDING-nyiso111-ramp-envelopes-2026-08-02.md §4) || nyiso-180 (2026-09-03, ZERO SOLVE, VERDICT UNCHANGED — K, armed in the keeper; evidence appended only): the armed envelopes were TESTED as a candidate carrier of nyiso-179 §6.1 un-dispatched in-the-money ST_GAS and are NOT the dominant term. build_ramp_groups puts NYISO ST_GAS in 11 measured two-sided plant-group envelopes. The pre-registered G2 was declared ONE-SIDED BEFORE IT RAN (the rows are per (plant, bucket) group while the committed artifact is a class aggregate — the same structure that invalidated nyiso-113 K3/K4 against system summed reserve_price), and it reads INCONCLUSIVE — PENDING SIDECAR, explicitly NOT an exoneration: the class delta never reaches 0.95x the 3,822 MW aggregate up-envelope (max 1,449/2,278/2,085 MW). A POST-HOC REPORT settles it on the merits anyway, by the ramp hypothesis own question: the withholding is SUSTAINED, not transient — 6,008/7,911/5,144 h >10%, median run 7/16.5/5 h, MAX RUN 137/2,650/270 h, 85/99/81% of withheld hours in runs >6 h — while every ST_GAS ramp group traverses cold-to-full in 1.5-3.0 h (median 2.39 h; up-envelope 0.34-0.65 of group capacity). A ramp row bounds the RATE of change, not the LEVEL, so it cannot hold a roughly constant ~1,000 MW gap open for 2,650 consecutive hours. RE-OPEN ONLY with per-group dispatch AND a mechanism for a LEVEL gap. Evidence: FINDING-nyiso180-st-gas-undispatch-2026-09-03.md §6, PREREG-nyiso180-st-gas-undispatch.md §2 G2, _nyiso180_ramp_report.json" },
