    diagnostics_plant_set: { cell: "I", ev: "caiso-155 §B/§D (7.884 TWh/yr HQ row now visible; nyiso_gas_commitment_bridge 5.31/3.14 pp G-06 false-FAIL averted via BRIDGE_MECHS) NYISO-175 (2026-09-02, ZERO SOLVE; docs/FINDING-nyiso175-ct-deficit-two-objects-2026-09-02.md sections 2.1, 2.2, 7 item 2). CELL UNCHANGED AT I -- the mechanism this cell registers is not impeached; what is added is a MEASURED REPRODUCIBILITY GAP in the artifact it produces, handed forward as a diagnostics-integrity lane. THE KEEPER'S COMMITTED D-2 IS NOT RE-DERIVABLE FROM COMMITTED ARTIFACTS. It was built at solve time on the run's own dispatch/<year>_P1.parquet (every model plant); that file is gitignored, so a HEAD recompute falls SILENTLY to the 100-plant run payload -- which covers only CEMS-metered plants and carries render_calibration_html's report-only CHP behind-the-meter add-back -- and moves class_total_twh by 28.9 % (CC_CHP), 34.3 % (CT_CHP), 95.3 % (ST_CHP) and 37.3 % (hydro) in 2025, with no warning anywhere in the artifact. The classes that survive are exactly the payload-covered ones ('' 0.005 %, ST_GAS 1.7 %, CC_REGULAR 1.8 %). This is the pjm-149 build_plant_matrices path divergence, live on a current keeper. PROOF THE COMMITTED ARTIFACT IS ON THE PARQUET PATH, off committed bytes alone: D-2's hydro equals class_hourly's to four decimals in all three years (26.6134 / 26.7390 / 24.0589) and D-2's '' bucket equals class_hourly nuclear + the 7.884 TWh HQ firm-import pseudo-unit to 0.005 %. PROPOSED REPAIR, ZERO SOLVE, CROSS-ISO: dispatch_source is already computed (legitimacy_diagnostics.py ~3012/3024) and used only in a coverage note -- stamping it into the D-2 block would close the gap. RELATED AND SETTLED HERE: the 13-17x D-2 vs class_hourly split disagreement nyiso-174 section 6 item 3 filed as a blocker is a GRAIN difference, not a defect in either artifact -- D-2's row is the PLANT and its label is the plant's most-common LP-unit plant_group, so East River (4 CT_CHP tranches vs 3 ST_CHP) is labelled CT_CHP and its ST_CHP energy is counted in D-2's CT_CHP denominator; the CT_CHP/ST_CHP deltas are equal and opposite to a residual of 0.0084 / 0.0271 / 0.0746 TWh. class_hourly is the identified per-class model artifact. The ST_CHP share_of_class > 1 is a unit-grain numerator over a plant-grain denominator -- the pathology run_d2's own docstring discloses -- and it can NEVER gate rule 20 [R-FORCED-BUDGET] because the three CHP classes are in D2_EXEMPT_CLASSES. DO-NOT-REDO the basis question." },
