    measured_offer_surface: { cell: "G", ev: "STAYS G. nyiso-245 2026-09-20 (0 solves for this mechanism, no arm shard) SATISFIED BOTH LIMBS OF nyiso-244's RE-OPEN CONDITION AND WAS REFUSED ANYWAY, ON A THIRD GATE — so that re-open condition is now SPENT and must not be cited again. Limb 1 (an econ/midcurve form): the form exists and is armed for another ISO — miso_offer_surface_measured, a within-unit own-curve price RISE on a position coordinate. Limb 2 (a validated mapping, or a form needing none): the SECOND branch holds by construction — both coordinates are within-unit, so masking cannot block it, which is MISO's own reasoning after miso-138 refuted its class bridge exactly as nyiso-244 section 4 refuted NYISO's. REACH ALSO CLEARS, decisively: the family's own row gate (offer_markup_hr > 0 and not base) tags 3,702.3 MW of the 4,715.7 MW object, 78.5% against the 50% bar nyiso-244 set and this session carried over unchanged — because gas_offer_net_revenue_margin is LIVE on NYISO's ECON bands (econ_low/econ_high sit above phys_* on CT_PEAKER, ST_GAS, CC_REGULAR, CC_CHP), so 298 of 715 rows carry the tag and they are econ-dominated. RULE 19 CLEARS: five armed non-base writers enumerated from the keeper's own run_config, zero tagged rows are also base rows, and the form is an ASSIGNMENT mc[row] := mc[base] + Delta, so it replaces rather than stacks; nyiso_zonal_loss_surface name-matched the screen and is adjudicated NOT a rung writer (it splits transmission chain links). WHAT REFUSES IT IS G3a, a corpus-shape test decided on the derived artifact alone and NOT on any residual (rule 1 [R-STRUCT]): the measured Delta ladder is non-monotone in 12 of 12 populated (gas x state) cells against an 80% bar — it rises to position 0.6-0.8 then collapses at the top, where the capacity-weighted median is $0.03-$1.62 — and its largest value ANYWHERE is $7.28/MWh. THE DIAGNOSTIC THEN SAYS WHY, cohort-free and composition-free (within-unit differences over gens present in BOTH windows, so the ~9.4 GW scope gap cancels exactly). Missed minus ordinary winter 2022, cap-weighted median $/MWh: the MARKET moves its curve BOTTOM +26.66 and its within-unit RISE +0.12; restricted to multi-block units (203 gens, 31,547 MW — every price taker excluded) BOTTOM +19.01 and RISE +1.03; the MODEL moves BOTTOM +40.00 and RISE +11.34. THE MARKET DOES NOT STEEPEN WITHIN UNITS AND THE MODEL ALREADY STEEPENS 11x MORE THAN IT DOES, so there is no conditional SHAPE object to transfer and a shape-only form is blind to the object BY CONSTRUCTION. What the market does instead is DISPERSE: its level response is +19 at the median but +112.05 at p75 and +231.59 at p90, while the model moves nearly every unit by the same ~40 (p75 +44.36) and none by more. RE-OPEN CONDITION, REPLACING nyiso-244's SPENT ONE: only a form whose object is the CROSS-UNIT DISPERSION of the conditional LEVEL response — the class miso_offer_spread_anchored / miso_offer_level_dispersion belongs to — and it enters as U and derives its own parameters from NYISO's own book (rule 28(d)). A within-unit SHAPE form is now refuted on NYISO's own corpus and must not be re-proposed. Rule 26 [R-DELETE]: the ScenarioConfig fields and applier written for the refused form were REVERTED, not committed default-off. docs/RESULT-nyiso245-the-object-is-level-dispersion-not-shape-2026-09-20.md" },
