    gas_electric_power_monthly_level: { cell: "K", ev: "PROMOTED TO THE KEEPER 2026-09-09 (session nyiso-fuelvintage-1, run 2026-09-09-nyiso-221-fuelvintage-span; cell I -> K). THE ARM IS ARMED IN NYISO'S KEEPER RECIPE AND IS MEASURED LP-INERT -- both halves of that sentence are the result. OWNER RULING 2026-09-09 (docs/handoffs/xiso-fuelvintage-per-iso-lp-prompts-2026-09-09.md ADDENDUM A7), verbatim: 'these should be promoted as keepers on both 860 and gas shape counts regardless of inertness' -- which WITHDRAWS the pre-A7 guidance this cell was first adjudicated under ('if it is near-inert leave the flag off'). Near-inertness is now a REPORTED PROPERTY, not a reason to withhold. The inertness measurement is UNCHANGED and is carried below verbatim; it was EXTENDED to the holdout years on the sanctioned reconstruction (replay_keeper.run_year_kwargs, the STRICT meta->kwarg mapping rather than the parameter-name filter the v3 phase-0 probe used): fuel_prices AND mc_base byte-identical, max|delta| = 0.0, in 2021 and 2022 as well as 2023, 2024 and 2025 (scripts/probes/nyiso_fuelvintage1_card1_holdout.py). That is what lets ONE set of solves serve both postures -- a flag-off touchpoint and a flag-on touchpoint are the SAME SOLVE, measured rather than inferred from the coverage table. WHAT ARMING BUYS, stated honestly: nothing measurable at HEAD, and structurally a FALLBACK LEVEL under the rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH] ordering (national annual < state-average monthly < measured hub index) -- in any month the Transco Z6 index does not cover, NYISO gas falls back to that month's MEASURED state-blended delivered cost instead of the annual trajectory x generic climatological shape. ZERO free parameters; the DOF ledger is carried verbatim from the superseded keeper and scripts/gen_nyiso214_attestation.py REFUSES to write the attestation if it is not. DO-NOT-REDO IS UNCHANGED AND STILL BINDS: re-arming cannot move a NYISO number while gas_hub_basis_overlay covers 12/12 months, so the only evidence that reopens this cell is a MONTH THE HUB INDEX DOES NOT COVER -- never a re-run. Evidence: docs/RESULT-nyiso-fuelvintage-1-2026-09-09.md, docs/ADDENDUM-nyiso-fuelvintage-1-promotion-2026-09-09.md. --- THE ORIGINAL ADJUDICATION, CARRIED VERBATIM --- nyiso-fuelvintage-1 (2026-09-09, ZERO LP \\u2014 ADJUDICATED PROVABLY LP-INERT BEFORE ANY SOLVE WAS SPENT; entered from O). PRE-REGISTERED in results/calibration/PRECOMMIT-nyiso-fuelvintage-1.md \\u00a72 before the measurement: 'C3b unchanged to three decimals, and more strongly the assembled generator gas price expected byte-identical'. MEASURED: with the flag armed on the keeper recipe (2026-09-07-nyiso-213-summer-seam), the assembled fuel_prices AND mc_base arrays are BYTE-IDENTICAL in 2023, 2024 and 2025 \\u2014 max|delta| = 0.0 in every year. Those arrays ARE the LP's input, so the LP is byte-identical and no dispatch answer needed buying (rule 29 [R-SCREEN] clause (0)); the planned SHARD F 2023 screen solve was NOT spent. WHY IT IS INERT, from the seam rather than from the residual: resolve.py applies the EP-level seam at :151, the F923 plant-monthly prints at :228 and apply_hub_basis_overlay at :229 \\u2014 the Transco Z6 hub index is the LAST word on gas price, after BOTH, and phase 0 measured it covering 12/12 months in every one of the seven years 2019-2025, so there is no month for the seam's level to survive into. (The handoff's account had the hub overlay superseding only the seam; it also supersedes the prints. The A2 written-cell census is the reason that matters here: the F923 print path writes only 56.738% of NYISO gas capacity-hours \\u2014 265 of 492 gas units, 35.982% of all cells \\u2014 NOT the ~100% MISO shows, so the prints alone would NOT have made this inert; the hub overlay is what does.) Hub vs the N3045 state blend, annual $/MMBtu: 2019 +0.040, 2020 -0.034, 2021 +0.533, 2022 +1.377, 2023 +0.432, 2024 +0.106, 2025 +1.180 (max month 5.107, Jan 2025) \\u2014 the keeper series runs ABOVE the state average in six of seven years, as downstate NYC gas should. THE ORDERING IS RIGHT. DO-NOT-REDO without a new measured series: re-arming this cannot move a NYISO number while gas_hub_basis_overlay covers 12/12 months, so a future test needs a month the hub index does NOT cover, not a re-run. Evidence: results/calibration/_nyiso_fuelvintage1_gate_t3.json (card1_ordering), _nyiso_fuelvintage1_phase0.json, scripts/probes/nyiso_fuelvintage1_gate_t3.py." },
