    dual_fuel_switching: { cell: "K", ev: "nyiso-179 (2026-09-03, ZERO SOLVE, VERDICT UNMOVED, NO PARAMETER TOUCHED): LINE CLOSED as the ST_GAS dear-hour lever, on rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH] executed rather than asserted: the ARMED cap already does the job nyiso-178 SS9.1 proposed a new mechanism for. Measured on the LP's own delivered-fuel arrays via an INPUT-SIDE A/B (resolve_fuel_prices on vs off, no LP): reach is 0.834 of ST_GAS LP capacity (7,424 of 8,902 MW keyed (plant_code, ST_GAS) in eia860.dual_fuel_plant_groups), and the cap bites hardest exactly where predicted -- 2025's top price decile, 0.0875 of bin-hours capped at a MW-weighted relief of $2.371/MMBtu, pulling delivered gas from $11.76 to $9.39 (a 20% cut in the class's dominant cost term). 2023/2024 bind at 0.0075/0.0432 with $0.281/$0.117 relief, i.e. the mechanism is correctly year-asymmetric. Both pre-registered legs clear (reach >= 0.50, top-decile binding >= 0.05). NO new fuel-side mechanism proposed; nothing armed or changed. RE-OPEN CONDITION: a keeper whose ST_GAS oil-parity reach falls below 0.50, or one in which the measured NY Harbor ULSD basis is shown wrong. Evidence: docs/FINDING-nyiso179-st-gas-offer-position-2026-09-03.md, results/calibration/PREREG-nyiso179-st-gas-offer-position.md, results/calibration/_nyiso179_st_gas_offer_position.json + _nyiso179_g1_robustness.json || nyiso-180 (2026-09-03, ZERO SOLVE, VERDICT UNCHANGED — K): a REAL committed-artifact DEFECT of this mechanism is measured and FIXED, and it is NOT the carrier of nyiso-179 §6.1. Because dual_fuel_oil_reattribution is armed, _dispatch_frame:455 relabels every oil-switched (gen, hour) to the POOLED klass oil, so class_hourly ST_GAS UNDERCOUNTS the class by the switched MWh while an ITM denominator counts every bin in every hour — a bias in exactly the observed direction, which is why it needed a gate, not a code read. Pre-registered G1 bounds it EXACTLY from both sides and reads SURVIVES: crediting ST_GAS with 100% of the pooled oil class moves the median ratio only 0.775→0.775 / 0.448→0.448 / 0.816→0.821 against the inherited 0.70 floor (switching occurs in just 24/72/192 h of 8,760; mean oil 17/48/144 MW). Instrument validated: the no-oil leg reproduces the nyiso-179 published medians to 0.0001 in all three years, and the switch mask is reconstructed EXACTLY with no re-derivation (apply_dual_fuel_pricing writes min(gas, oil) in place, so a switched hour is precisely pre-min > post-min). THE DEFECT IS FIXED GENERALLY, not for NYISO: the new hourly/class_band_hourly_<year>.parquet sidecar keys on the PRE-re-attribution plant group (a new klass_base column) and carries mw_oil, so the class_hourly view is exactly reproducible in both directions and no dual-fuel class is undercounted again in any ISO. Evidence: FINDING-nyiso180-st-gas-undispatch-2026-09-03.md §5 + §8, PREREG-nyiso180-st-gas-undispatch.md §2 G1, _nyiso180_st_gas_undispatch.json.." },
