    temp_dependent_derate: { cell: "G", ev: "nyiso-111 (ex-ante refusal on NYISO's own conduct, no solve — FINDING-nyiso111-ramp-envelopes-2026-08-02.md §2). CELL RE-READ AND HELD AT G 2026-09-14 (nyiso-234, ZERO LP, nothing armed, keeper unchanged; docs/FINDING-nyiso234-tail-gas-is-unobserved-2026-09-14.md §1), on the owner-referred question of whether nyiso-233's tail-headroom measurement is new evidence defeating the refusal. IT IS NOT, and the ruling rests on TWO INDEPENDENT LEGS. (1) IDENTIFICATION, nyiso-111's own basis, UNDEFEATED: the refusal was that NYISO's CAMPD conduct cannot MEASURE an ambient slope (2 of 15 plants identify; sign INVERTS at -0.00745/C, capability rising with temperature, i.e. the NYC A/C dispatch shape; the one near-pinned plant measures no response at all, r=0.006; phase validation fails at best lag -5 h). nyiso-233 measured a RESIDUAL (3,390-6,247 MW idle thermal in the top-1 % actual-price hours), which is MOTIVE, not identification — and nyiso-111's own stated re-open condition ('a future intake with an actual capability instrument — unit DMNC test results, or a plant pinned at capability') remains UNMET, no such instrument having entered the repo. Arming on a residual with the slope unidentified is the rule 1 [R-STRUCT] move the refusal exists to forbid, and rule 21 [R-DOF] would have no identification source to ledger. (2) A NEW AND INDEPENDENT REACH BAR that did not exist in August and that no slope can rescue: the COMMITTED curve is IDENTICALLY 1.0 in cold hours — the hinge form is 1 - slope*max(0, Tmax - temp_derate_ref_c) with temp_derate_ref_c = 15.0 C (flat at or below the hinge), and the mean-anchored form exceeds 1.0 below the annual mean and is clipped back by np.clip(availability,0,1). So the share of the tail gap below the hinge is a CEILING ON REACH AT ANY SLOPE, and measured on the ACTUAL-selected tail taking the WARMEST zone per hour (the most generous reading, hence a LOWER bound) it is 79.8 / 49.4 / 38.4 / 15.8 % in 2022/23/24/25, stable across tail depth (2022 77-86 % at the 0.5/1/2/5 % cuts). IN 2022 — THE ONLY YEAR THAT FAILS C3a (-11.6 %) — THE MECHANISM CANNOT TOUCH FOUR-FIFTHS OF THE OBJECT. The object is BOTH-SEASONS (DJF carries 76.2/46.0/36.1/15.3 % of the tail gap, JJAS 19.0/42.9/53.1/82.3 %), and a hot-weather-only instrument cannot cover a both-seasons object whatever its parameterization. Probe scripts/probes/_nyiso234_tail_season_reach.py (argument = tail depth %). NOTHING WAS ARMED, no solve was spent, and the cell is NOT routed to a '.' neighbour — the whole availability family is closed on ARITHMETIC in the same finding's §2 (nyiso-227's measured sub-5-day family peaks at 1,653-2,351 MW against 3,390-6,247 MW of idle headroom, i.e. 2-3x too small, and would have to eat that headroom before removing a single MW the model uses)." },
