    hydro_dispatch_envelope: { cell: "K", ev: "nyiso-92 / FINDING-nyiso92-hydro-capability-envelope-2026-07-28.md; nyiso-218 §8 (residual localized) / nyiso-219 (successor DATA question answered — FINDING-nyiso219-hydro-daily-driver-data-question-2026-09-07.md, DECISION-CARD-nyiso219-hydro-within-month-allocation-2026-09-07.md, probes nyiso219_hydro_daily_driver_census.py + nyiso219_posthoc_overresponse.py); nyiso-219 Option-C charter (owner-instructed 2026-09-07 — CHARTER-nyiso219-hydro-budget-period-2026-09-07.md, probe nyiso219_pondage_feasibility_census.py)",
      note: "K UNCHANGED, keeper UNCHANGED, NO cell letter moves — annotation only, ZERO LP, no field, no arm, no marker. nyiso-218 §8 showed this family succeeds precisely in the two dimensions it constrains (month energy r ~1.000, hour-of-day r ~0.98) and that ALL the residual has retreated into WITHIN-MONTH day-to-day allocation (r 0.207/0.248/0.392, 0.358 on the 2022 touchpoint), which no armed mechanism touches. nyiso-219 answered the open DATA question it handed over and CLOSED TWO OF THE THREE CANDIDATE ROUTES ON MEASUREMENT, so no future session re-spends on them. (1) THE DAILY INFLOW DRIVER EXISTS AND IS EXCELLENT AND CANNOT CLOSE THIS: 163/163 plants resolve to a published EIA-860 'Name of Water Source' (100.00 % of 4,681.0 MW), every material basin has a USGS NWIS daily-discharge record at 100.0 % coverage / 100 % approved / public domain — and measured basin discharge reaches within-month daily r 0.243 mean (0.095-0.327), BELOW the keeper's own 0.392 in 2023 and 0.358 in 2022. Cause: 71.38 % of fleet MW sits on REGULATED GREAT-LAKES OUTFLOW (Niagara 51.89 %, St Lawrence 19.48 %) whose within-month daily flow CV is 4.01 % / 3.11 % against a runoff river's 56.48 %; Niagara's own mean r is 0.079 on 51.9 % of the MW, while the best single flow predictor is a 3.95 %-of-MW Adirondack cascade at 0.265. Robust: five independent D-B constructions span mean r 0.217-0.267, none above 0.327 in any year, and the pre-registered MW weighting is GENEROUS to the hypothesis (energy weighting would score lower). (2) THE MULTI-YEAR CLIMATOLOGICAL DAILY SHAPE IS PROVABLY EMPTY: leave-one-year-out day-of-year climatology, mean r 0.031, max |r| 0.074 — the only construction that regenerates forward, so rule 13 [R-MEASURED] fails the inflow route on its own terms. (3) WHAT IT FOUND INSTEAD (post-hoc, moves no gate, model years 2023-2025 only): the ACTUAL fleet tracks daily LOAD (mean r 0.308) BETTER than it tracks measured FLOW (0.243), while the keeper tracks load at r 0.647/0.686/0.616 with 1.86-2.25x the actual's within-month daily amplitude. THE MODEL IS NOT MISSING A DRIVER — IT HAS THE RIGHT DRIVER AND RESPONDS ~2x TOO HARD, because nothing bounds how much water the LP may move between the days of a month. Ceiling on any driver-based route: load+flow together, fitted with hindsight, reach mean multiple r 0.402 against a keeper already at 0.207-0.392. Successor object handed to the owner as a missing BOUND (published usable storage / Niagara Treaty scenic-flow schedule / IJC Plan-2014), with the rule-13 trap named in advance: a bound set at the actual's own measured sd (5.7-8.0 % of daily mean) would be outcome-derived and is forbidden. Instrument self-check: the keeper's within-month r reconstructs to 0.3916/0.2476/0.2066 vs nyiso-218's committed 0.392/0.248/0.207. (4) OPTION C CHARTERED BY THE OWNER (2026-09-07, still ZERO LP, still no field and no cell move): the successor is the BUDGET PERIOD, not a new water-value term — the LP ALREADY computes a water value (the hydro budget row's dual) and the defect is that there is exactly ONE PER MONTH, so any price difference between days of the same month is pure arbitrage profit with no offsetting cost. THE SUCCESSOR WAS NAMED IN WRITING ON 2026-07-25 (FINDING-nyiso-overnight-marginal-is-hydro-water-value section 6: 'the physically faithful representation of a run-of-river fleet with hours-to-days of pondage is a SHORTER BUDGET PERIOD (daily/pondage-duration), not a ceiling on top of a monthly budget'; logged at calibration-log/nyiso.md 582-583) and NEVER TAKEN UP — no field, no matrix row, no charter until now. STRUCTURAL FINDING THAT MAKES IT CHEAP: _build_hydro_rows is ALREADY GENERAL over budget periods (it takes an arbitrary (T,) period index and an (n_hydro, n_periods) energy matrix; n_months = energy.shape[1]), so shortening the period is a RE-INDEXING and rows.py needs NO CHANGE — the 12-wide assumption lives in data/hydro.py and the plumbing. FEASIBILITY CENSUS (post-hoc, no predictions, sources already committed): HILARRI v4 links 163/163 NYISO hydro plants (100.0 pct of MW), 152 carry a NID dam id (98.5 pct of MW — Robert Moses Niagara NY16253, St Lawrence NY00678), so the pondage-storage route is a BOUNDED intake against 152 named dams rather than an open research question; ORNL EHA FY2024 Mode matches 163/163 and puts 78.02-84.24 pct of fleet MW on a PEAKING-component label (Niagara 'Run-of-river/Peaking' 52.80 pct, St Lawrence 'Peaking'), i.e. sub-monthly pondage — and that census CORROBORATES nyiso-111's hydro_ror_split refusal rather than disturbing it, since Niagara carries exactly the hybrid label the refusal turned on. MISSING and named: NID storage volumes (not in repo), head (in none of EHA/HILARRI/NID), and the LICENSED OPERATING RANGE (NID normal storage is a reservoir volume, so using it literally OVERSTATES pondage and makes the mechanism too weak, not too strong). REFUSED IN ADVANCE: any period-length sweep against the gates (rule 1 fitted-mechanism selection), any pin to measured NG:WAT, and any STACKING on hydro_dispatch_envelope — rule 19 requires REPLACE or RECONCILE, and this cell is measured binding in 27-42 pct of hours, so the overlap is the charter's hard part and is an open owner question (charter section 9 Q2). Charter authorizes NOTHING; three owner questions open." },
