    scuc_load_pocket_commitment: { cell: "G", ev: "nyiso-192 (2026-09-05): TWO MORE OBJECTS LAND ON THIS CELL, neither re-opens it (nyiso-97 section 5 / nyiso-160 stand). (a) With NYC steam priced at any basis above the hub, the model's NYC steam collapses to its floor (C8 by construction) -- the market's 3.0 TWh of NYC steam in 2024 is out-of-market commitment, the offer-side restatement of nyiso-187. (b) The Astoria merit-panel arm (2026-09-05-nyiso-192-astoria-panel): the 0.81 TWh of ST_GAS a more accurate availability envelope removes in 2024 lands 0.35 on CC_REGULAR and flips C1-2024 (+3.33 -> +3.68 TWh) -- the within-family fill onto the class this cell's absence leaves open. docs/FINDING-nyiso192-frontier-adjudication-2026-09-05.md sections 3-4. || nyiso-190 (2026-09-05, ZERO SOLVE ON THIS OBJECT; docs/FINDING-nyiso190-cc2024-displacement-provenance-2026-09-05.md, PREREG-nyiso190-cc2024-displacement-provenance.md pushed before the first number). CELL UNCHANGED AT G -- no re-open attempted, none recommended, and the nyiso-97 section 5 bar is the reason this session could never supply one: it forbids identifying the pocket requirement from observed unit conduct, and this measurement IS observed unit conduct (pre-registered stop S2). WHAT CHANGES IS THE CELL ON THE OTHER SIDE: the C1-2024 CC_REGULAR excess is NO LONGER wholly attributable to this cell's disposition. The nyiso-189 promotion's justifying clause ('the NYC steam it displaces is what the market committed anyway') is MEASURED AND REFUTED on the keeper's own registered dispatch: the market did have the displaced units on (B1 s_online 0.839 of removed MWh at the 2 % bar; 0.750 / 0.834 in 2023 / 2025) but the model was running them HARDER than the market did -- 78.1 % of the displaced TWh moved TOWARD the plants' measured annual output (B2 w_away 0.219 CAMPD / 0.216 EIA-923, both bases agreeing; 0.139 / 0.375 in 2023 / 2025), so the displacement RELIEVED a model over-run rather than deepening a market-committed deficit. B4: only 0.42 of the 2024 displaced TWh is downstate steam/cogen, below the pre-committed 0.50 naming bar, so the set is not what the clause names (0.76 TWh CC_CHP / 0.46 CC_REGULAR / 0.30 ST_GAS; NYC 0.74 / Capital-Hudson 0.71 / Upstate-West 0.21). B3 HOLDS -- the arm moves the six-class gas family total by 0.042 TWh at +1.87 from actual against a +/-3.82 band -- so it IS a within-family reallocation, just not from the class the clause named. The CT half of the nyiso-187 disposition (CT_PEAKER -1.59, CT_CHP -1.20 TWh in 2024) stands verbatim and is untouched. Owner card: docs/DECISION-CARD-nyiso190-cc2024-cell-disposition-2026-09-05.md -- it deliberately does NOT put the re-open-G question, because the premise it rested on is refuted. || PRIOR EVIDENCE (nyiso-187) PRESERVED: nyiso-187 (2026-09-04, ZERO SOLVE ON THIS OBJECT; docs/FINDING-nyiso187-ct-steam-merit-position-2026-09-04.md §2): CELL UNCHANGED AT G — no re-open attempted; what is added is a SECOND independent confirmation from the receiving end, on a pre-registered bar. Every deficit MW of NYC / LI / CH CT_PEAKER, CT_CHP and ST_GAS in 2024 was filled from the model's cheapest un-run capacity at the LP's INSTALLED offer (unit_hourly.mc, the nyiso-181 instrument) and bucketed against the model zonal price and the actual RT price: OUT OF THE MONEY AT BOTH (bucket B) carries 0.85 / 0.83 (CT_PEAKER NYC / LI), 0.88 / 0.89 (CT_CHP), 0.89 / 0.75 / 0.57 (ST_GAS LI / CH / NYC); in-the-money-yet-unrun is nil (<= 0.011, reproducing nyiso-181's retirement per zone); no measured input (delivered CT gas, heat rate, carbon) departs from its source. Owner = out-of-market commitment. Post-hoc, labelled: with every markup removed, 96 % (NYC) / 73 % (LI) of the CT_PEAKER deficit capacity would be in the money at the model's own price — the separator for that class is the owner-accepted markup stack (nyiso-96 trade), while CT_CHP / ST_GAS are out of merit on bare cost. The 2024 CC_REGULAR cell is therefore a disposition behind this cell, not a lane. || PRIOR EVIDENCE: nyiso-97 (docs/FINDING-nyiso97-load-pocket-identification-2026-07-29.md); nyiso-160: the authorized Leg-2 AORR intake (INTAKE-SPEC-nyiso156 §2) STOPPED WITH CAUSE at access — the owner cannot produce the MyNYISO files; the nyiso-97 re-open bar stands unchanged (results/calibration/FINDING-nyiso160-leg2-stop-and-tpaudit-2026-08-30.md) NYISO-175 (2026-09-02, ZERO SOLVE; docs/FINDING-nyiso175-ct-deficit-two-objects-2026-09-02.md section 3.3). CELL UNCHANGED AT G -- no re-open attempted, the nyiso-97 bar and the nyiso-163b permanent access closure both stand. What is added is an INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION of the diagnosis this cell carries: measured on the CORRECTED CAMPD class construction (scripts/lib/campd_measured_classes.py), at a different online bar (2 % of the class's own demonstrated p99.5) and on a different keeper than nyiso-90/91/96 used, CT_PEAKER's run lengths still MATCH (median 8/7/7 h model against 9/7/10 h measured) while its starts are 2.5-4.9x too few (102/93/156 against 399/457/293) and its on-hours 805/779/1,556 against 5,927/5,093/6,803; only 37.8 / 28.2 / 43.2 % of measured class energy falls in an hour the model runs the class at all. On the pre-registered B5 rule CT_PEAKER is LEVEL-limited (q90 model / q90 anchored-measured 0.050 / 0.053 / 0.369) -- the OPPOSITE signature to CT_CHP's RESPONSE deficit in the same lane, which is why the two classes must not be treated as one object again. Rule 19: CT_PEAKER is COMPLETELY UNFORCED and COMPLETELY UNDERATED -- D-2 forced energy exactly 0.0000 TWh in all three years, ct_mustrun_per_plant False, nyiso_incity_commitment_obligation False (nyiso-83 R), nyiso_gas_bridge_ct False (nyiso-90 R), and _generic_unit_outage_target returns None for the class by design. The session's pre-registered guard S4 forbade opening a CT_PEAKER lever and none was opened." },
