    neiso_net_icr_requirement: { cell: ".", fc: ".", ev: "ISO-exclusive (capx D40): NYISO's requirement is the NYSRC IRM × the NYCA translation factor (R5a); the per-capability-year IRM series is a NYISO-side analogue not adjudicated here (rule 25)." },
    pjm_accreditation_design_vintage: { cell: ".", fc: ".", ev: "ISO-exclusive (capx D48): NYISO accredits on UCAP (1 - EFORd, the registry default) in every year and its requirement is the NYSRC IRM x the NYCA translation factor (R5a) — no design-vintage switch to devintage; the per-capability-year IRM/translation series is the NYISO-side analogue, not adjudicated here (rule 25)." },
    pjm_vre_accreditation_vintage: { cell: ".", fc: ".", ev: "ISO-exclusive (capx D75-R): NYISO accredits intermittents at the per-capability-year Capacity Accreditation Factors already wired as single-point curves (RENEWABLE_ELCC_CURVES_BY_ISO[NYISO], the 2025-2026 Final CAFs) -- the same vintage question in NYISO is the CAF SERIES by capability year, which is the NYISO lane's own object (alongside nyiso_requirement_vintage_factors), not a transfer of this cell (rule 25). Inert by construction." },
    pjm_thermal_accreditation_vintage: { cell: ".", fc: ".", ev: "ISO-exclusive (capx D84): NYISO accredits thermal on UCAP/DMNC with per-capability-year Capacity Accreditation Factors, and is absent from THERMAL_ACCREDITATION_BASIS_BY_ISO so the elcc_class_rating branch is never taken. The same vintage question in NYISO is the thermal CAF SERIES by capability year, which is the NYISO lane's own object (alongside nyiso_requirement_vintage_factors), not a transfer of this cell (rule 25). Inert by construction." },
    pjm_demand_response_supply: { cell: ".", fc: ".", ev: "ISO-exclusive (capx D48): NYISO's SCR program is not netted from the peak by the registry (no ADEQUACY_DEMAND_RESPONSE_FRACTION_BY_ISO entry) and is not counted as supply; an SCR supply-side series would enter NYISO as U only through a NYISO lane's own derivation (rule 25)." },
    capacity_market_supply_clearing: { cell: ".", fc: "U", ev: "UNTESTED by design (capx D57, design §4.9): NYISO's spot capacity market literally administers price = demand curve(supplied UCAP) — the ONE ISO whose real mechanism IS 'evaluate the curve at a census quantity' (D28 §4) — so its clearing half is a supply-CENSUS question (D52's object; the locality half is D59's), not an offer-stack one. This gate would be the wrong mechanism here; it stays U with no transfer (rule 25)." },
    capacity_going_forward_bar_published: { cell: ".", fc: "U", ev: "UNTESTED, no transfer (rule 25 / 28d -- capx D62, 2026-09-06): NYISO's ICAP market does cap a supplier's offer against a going-forward-cost benchmark -- the Mitigation Measures' Reference Levels and the buyer-side / exit-mitigation exemption tests -- but those are unit-specific reviewed levels, not a published generic technology-class default an owner may elect. The nearest published class quantities NYISO carries in this repo are the locality Gross-CONE / demand-curve parameters (capx D59), which are an ENTRY cost basis, not an avoidable going-forward bar, and using them as one would be a category error. A NYISO instance therefore needs its own intake and its own identification in a NYISO lane. PJM's verdict fills nothing here (rule 25). No NYISO partition exists in data/raw/capacity-market/avoidable-cost-rate/, so an armed gate is inert for every unit." },
    capacity_adequacy_requirement_published: { cell: ".", fc: "U", ev: "UNTESTED, no transfer (rule 25 / 28d -- capx D67, 2026-09-06): NYISO's NYCA requirement is genuinely of this kind -- an absolute UCAP MW bar per capability year -- but it is ALREADY addressed by its own pair of gates, capx D52's nyiso_requirement_forecast_peak and nyiso_requirement_vintage_factors, which reach the same seam (gross_adequacy_requirement_mw) by replacing the requirement's PEAK with the published NYSRC ICAP-market forecast peak and its FACTOR with the capability year's adopted IRM x (1 - derate). That is the NYISO instance of the same repair, decomposed rather than absolute, and it is armed for NYISO. Arming this gate on top would be two mechanisms for one phenomenon (rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]); no NYISO reliability_requirement row is intaken and the gate is inert by construction." },
    capacity_no_default_cap_convention: { cell: ".", fc: "U", ev: "UNTESTED, no transfer (rule 25 / 28d — capx D74, 2026-09-06): NYISO's ICAP mitigation uses unit-specific Reference Levels, not a published elective technology-class default (the D62 NYISO cell), so no class can lack a default cap in a table NYISO does not publish; the predicate is False for every unit and the gate is inert by construction (and requires the D62 bar gate, inert here). PJM's verdict fills nothing; a NYISO instance needs its own intake and identification in a NYISO lane." },
