    nyiso_requirement_vintage_factors: { cell: ".", fc: "K", ev: "ARMED FOR NYISO 2026-09-05 by OWNER RULING Q41 (director sitting r#37), executed by capx D60, together with nyiso_requirement_forecast_peak (its A/B sibling; D52 §8(1) recommended ARM BOTH) -- iso_configs._nyiso_config default_scenario_overrides, rule 25; the ScenarioConfig default STAYS False and it remains a SEPARATE gate so either can be disarmed alone. On the 2026-2030 t1f horizon, which is entirely beyond NYSRC Table D.2, the hold-last limb is the whole effect: 1.244 x 0.870 = 1.0823, +0.24 % over the shipped composite. Verdict K on the D52 measured record. capx D52 (2026-09-04), FINDING-capx-d52-2026-09-04.md -- BUILT, DEFAULT-OFF, MEASURED WITH nyiso_requirement_forecast_peak in the one A/B arm nyiso-t1h-d52-devintage (key 911371a8cf23d5c3), NOT ARMED. The zero-solve decomposition on the arm's seam peak (PREDECL-capx-d52-2026-09-04.md P1; instrument docs/handoffs/d52/): the factors half alone moves the seam requirement -40 / -604 / +83 MW in 2023 / 2024 / 2025 (the adopted 20.0 / 22.0 / 24.4 % x (1 - 0.1014 / 0.1321 / 0.1300) pair vs the shipped 1.244 x 0.8679) -- 2024 the one in-window year it lowers the bar, D45 item 2's stated sign -- while the peak half alone moves it +3,680 / +2,755 / +2,295 MW; BOTH reproduce Table D.2 to < 1 MW. Hold-last beyond 2025/26 as the last published pair (1.244 x 0.870 = 1.0823, +0.24 % over the composite -- the golden's 2026+ requirement essentially untouched, the D40 exposure split). The shipped composite ratio stays pinned to the 2024-25 derate (a rule-23 re-derivation onto the 2025-26 row is routed to the owner in the finding, not smuggled in). fc O: the owner arms or declines; separate gate so either half can be armed alone." },
    locality_capacity_curves: { cell: ".", fc: "I", ev: "capx D59 (2026-09-05), FINDING-capx-d59-2026-09-05.md -- BUILT, DEFAULT-OFF, MEASURED, INERT ON THIS RECORD, NOT ARMED. A/B: the D52 curve-ON recipe replayed at the D59 HEAD as the CONTROL (nyiso-t1h-d59-control, key 589f031432b6dc7d -- the SAME key as the committed D52 bundle; 9 min) vs the ARM nyiso-t1h-d59-locality (+ locality_capacity_curves; key 4bb6dd6a798147b2; 9 min). WHAT THE ARM MEASURED (ledger block locality_capacity): NYC positions 1.115 / 1.107 / 1.147 in 2023 / 2024 / 2025 on the ICAP Manual §2.6 identity against the published 1.026 / 1.057 / 1.078 (SOM summer margins; 2025 = the implied reading, the printed 2025 row being a carry-over of 2024) -- +8.8 / +5.0 / +6.9 pts LONG, the model's NYC ICAP census (9,959 / 9,543 / 9,543 MW incl. Linden Cogen + Bayonne EC, which the fleet already places in Zone J) sitting +727 / +824 / +838 MW above the Gold Book Table III-2a Zone-J summer capability (the 2023-24 Peaker-Rule exit set the 2020-vintage fleet still carries + 2-3 % of DMNC/eligibility); NYC locality curve at those positions $56.3 / $61.0 / $25.7/kW-yr vs the NYCA leg $63.3 / $48.0 / $28.6 ⇒ the §5.15.2 max settles NYC at NYCA in 2023 and 2025 and at $61.0 in 2024 (a year in which nothing fails); LI 1.158 / 1.169 / 1.153 vs published 1.131 / 1.117 / 1.122 (+2.7 / +5.2 / +3.1 pts), LI curve $3.6-8.0 ⇒ NYCA every year (the SOM's own reading). FC-3: the arm is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the control on every score row (retire.total 3.360 GW +96 %, gas_st 1.904 GW all 2025 -- NYC 1,266.6 / Capital_Hudson 495.8 / Upstate_West 141.5, false 2.160 / 0.643, recall 1/1, LOYO false 1.928 / 2.178 / 0.353, T-R10a/b FAIL/FAIL, additions gas_cc 1.0 / gas_ct 0 / storage 0) -- the 2025 NYC cohort fails at the same NYCA $26.6 leg because the NYC curve at 1.147 pays LESS than NYCA. P9 (a) NO +96 % / (b) NO 0.643 / (c) YES ⇒ the NYCA curve stays OFF. The control differs from the committed D52 bundle (589f, D52 HEAD) only by upstream drift: the 2025 gas_st cohort 1,801 -> 1,904 MW (NYC 946 -> 1,267), the new D32-R4 plant_release_precision section, co2 -0.0005 % -- the input-vintage class D52 itself recorded vs D45-R. Pre-declaration graded: P1 resolved to its stated ALTERNATIVE branch (NYC position > 1.132 ⇒ byte-identical FC-3), P4 MISS in 2023 / 2025 (the census, +8.8 / +6.9 pts), P6 HIT (settled/spot 0.22-0.43, limb (iii) FAILS as pre-stated), P3 / P5 HIT. Verdict I: the mechanism is structurally the market's own (rule 1) and reproduces its published rows, but on this record it changes nothing; the object it surfaces is the NYC CENSUS (+5-9 pts) plus the shared ARV-at-1.0 annualization (a CR-3 object) -- both routed. Re-opens with new evidence on either. Backcast lane n/a (the field coerces to its default in a plain backcast)." },
