    ccs_retrofit_screen: { cell: "K", fc: "K", ev: "capx D87 (2026-09-08, docs/handoffs/FINDING-capx-d87-2026-09-08.md), SCN ruling S19 card D-15: THE SCREEN COULD NOT SEE A CLEAN-TIER DUAL AT ALL, AND NOW CAN. Before D87 apply_ccs_retrofit priced each continuation's certificate through effective_eac_price_for_unit alone -- the legacy per-fuel scalar and the exogenous premium -- while its two SIBLING screens (retirements.py:3634 step 3, new_entry.py:1202 step 5) folded a third leg, clean_credit_for_zone, off the clean_attribute_price_by_fuel seam; evolve_fleet had no parameter to hand it to step 2. Because a federal CES TARGET row carries a ZERO premium by construction (__post_init__ refuses the two together), attr_post collapsed to the eac_price_gas_cc_ccs default of 0.0 and the $50/MWh ACP bought the retrofit screen NOTHING. MEASURED ON THE COMMITTED RECORD: NYISO CES-T80's cumulative gas_cc_ccs is 2,984.4 / 5,255.9 / 6,255.9 MW at 2028/29/30 -- IDENTICAL TO REF, i.e. to no policy at all -- while CES-P20's $20 premium bought +1,475.8 MW by 2030. A stronger instrument at a higher price produced a smaller response than a weaker one, purely from which code path carried it. THE REPAIR is one seam and zero free parameters (rules 19/21/24/25): fold clean_credit_for_zone into BOTH attr_unabated and attr_post through the existing max(), threaded from evolve.py:664 as a None-default keyword; None credits 0.0 so every backcast, hindcast and premium-era forecast is byte-identical, and zero cache keys move (a runtime prior-year value, not a config field; neither ccs.py nor evolve.py is a solve_surface registry). SCREENED AS AN A/B AT HEAD, both arms concurrent, NYISO CES-T80 2026-2030, key eb1b0e1df942db47 in both, control = the arm's exact parent commit in an isolated worktree -- a control SOLVE rather than the committed bundle because the G-DRIFT hunk audit (34 commits / 62 files / 3,576 non-comment lines) found exactly ONE LIVE hunk for a NYISO forecast, SPP-49's unconditional simple-cycle heat-rate floor at 3 plants / 19.0 MW, and rule 29(b) says a LIVE hunk earns one. THE CONTROL REPRODUCED THE COMMITTED CAMPAIGN IN ALL THREE RETROFIT YEARS TO 0.04 MW, so that hunk moved the decision by 0.000 MW. RESULT: 6 of 7 pre-registered gates PASS. G1, the identity, passes to the cent -- arm attr_post = 47.50 = ACP 50.00 x federal_ces_ccs_capture_fraction 0.95 in 2028 and 2029 against 0.0 in the control, attr_unabated 0.0 in every year of both. Retrofit deltas +15.065 / +728.338 / +384.227 MW; cumulative 6,255.940 -> 7,383.569 MW, i.e. +1,127.6 MW of capture capacity the target row had been paying for and not getting. G3 (3 GW/yr cap) PASS at 2,999.880; G4 (2026-2027 byte-identity) PASS on every ledger key; G5 14/14 invariants PASS in both arms; G6 by construction + 7 seam tests, no LP; G7 (the D88 duplicate-unit_id census, pre-registered as the substitute for D88's guard) PASS -- 53 retrofitted ids in the arm vs 33 in the control and no collision. THE REASON IS NARROWER THAN 'NYISO USES CAMPD IDS', corrected at unit grain before the bundles were lost: both arms carry TWO legacy-form representative retrofits (gas_cc_h_class_NYC 1.8 MW in 2028, gas_cc_h_class_Upstate_West 1,000.0 MW in 2030), and the 2030 one sits in exactly the D88 trigger sequence -- an economic gas_cc entry of 1,000 MW lands in Upstate_West in 2029, is re-minted to the representative id at the next aggregate_fleet, and THAT unit is retrofitted in 2030 keeping the id. It does not collide ONLY because 2030 is the horizon's last year, the same shape D88 recorded for ERCOT ff-t1f-d65br. D87 neither creates nor worsens it (the legacy pair is byte-identical between arms; all 20 extra conversions are CAMPD per-plant), but on a T3-length NYISO horizon this pair WOULD collide -- so D88's guard is owed more sharply than a NYISO-clean census suggests (rule 25: NYISO-scoped, transfers nowhere). G2 FAILS BY THE LETTER ON 2029 BY 0.338 MW and the cause is the lane's own rounding: the bound WAS the cap headroom, transcribed from the rounded committed 2.272 GW (3.000-2.272=0.728) when the true headroom is 728.458 -- the miss stands on the record, is not re-derived, and the judgement is the owner's. THE PRE-SOLVE BRACKET PREDICTION MISSED, AND THAT IS THE REAL RESULT: the arm's 2030 cumulative landed at 7,383.6 MW, BELOW the (7,731.7, 7,890.3) premium bracket, because A TARGET ROW IS NOT A CONSTANT PREMIUM. Its dual is the LP's own marginal cost of the last credit -- capped at the ACP while the standard cannot be met (2027, 2028 short by 19.0 and 8.4 points), and COLLAPSING the moment it binds. The arm's own 2030 ledger reveals the 2029 endogenous dual as $7.5636/MWh (attr_post 7.18544 / 0.95), an 85 % fall in one year, which no committed artifact could supply. REPORTED AT FULL MAGNITUDE, NOT SMOOTHED: in-ISO CO2 is NOT monotone -- +0.1178 Mt at 2028 and +0.0328 at 2030 against -0.0340 at 2029 -- because the arm displaces zero-rated IMPORTS (-0.051 / -0.159 TWh) with in-ISO generation under the campaign's standing leakage disclosure; and at 2030 the arm holds +1,127.6 MW more gas_cc_ccs while generating exactly the same gas_cc_ccs energy, read as the marginal low-CF hosts converting last and ROUTED rather than asserted." },
    ccs_retrofit_capex_co2_scaling: { cell: ".", fc: "K", ev: "ARMED AS THE DEFAULT POSTURE 2026-09-05 by OWNER RULING Q42 (director sitting r#37), executed by capx D60 -- the ScenarioConfig default flips False -> True for ALL SIX ISOs ((b'-1) declared flip; see the ERCOT / NEISO / PJM / MISO cells for the measured A/Bs). K BY POSTURE, NOT BY TRANSFER (rule 25): the arm carries no other ISO's number -- every term is an already-cited constant sized against captured_ref 0.32319 t/MWh -- and this ISO's OWN t1f evidence is being produced by capx D60's re-solve, appended to this cell when it lands. ZERO-SOLVE CEILING CENSUS run by D60 for this ISO (the D50 §1 instrument, PREDECL-capx-d60-2026-09-05.md §6.5): NYISO shows the same carbon-priced signature -- at $27.06 / $28.96 / $30.98 per t the scaled bar moves 11.13 -> 11.14 GW clearing (nothing) and seam 2 removes 4.31 GW of CHP from an 11.20 GW eligible pool, leaving 6.86 GW -- so 2028 and 2029 stay at the 3 GW/yr cap and 2030 is pre-declared BELOW it once two capped years exhaust the non-CHP pool (control converts 2,994.7 / 2,997.1 / 2,979.7 MW, of which 20 / 8 / 3 rows are CHP). capx D50 (2026-09-04): built default-off, not solved for this ISO in the D50 lane; enters as U — a verdict needs this ISO's own solve (rule 25). Blast-radius key recorded in FINDING-capx-d50-2026-09-04.md. Backcast lane n/a (the screen is gated 2028)." },
