    entry_vre_zone_selection: { cell: "U", fc: "U", ev: "capx D33 minted the row (2026-09-02) and armed the gate for MISO ONLY (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]); this ISO is UNTESTED and byte-identical (ScenarioConfig default stays False). The identification that would open this cell is this ISO's OWN: whether its RENEWABLE_ZONE_ALLOCATION bucket is materially unrepresentative of where its market actually builds, and whether its RPS/clean rows are zone-restricted enough for the bucket to change the attribute credit. MISO is the extreme case (its bucket is the ONE zone no compliance region admits); an ISO with a single footprint-wide REC product has no attribute leg to gain and would move only on the price/CF legs.", },
    fossil_announced_exits: { cell: ".", fc: "O", ev: "ARMED AS THE DEFAULT 2026-09-03 by OWNER RULING Q30 (r#31 2026-09-02), executed by capx D44 (FINDING-capx-d44-fossil-dates-arm-2026-09-03.md): the ScenarioConfig default flips False -> True in ALL SIX lanes — the ruling arms a POSTURE, which carries no ISO's fitted numbers, so rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] is satisfied by construction rather than by withholding the channel. U -> O, NOT K: this ISO's forecast lane now RUNS the channel (armed, in play) but holds NO measured verdict for it — the D42 evidence is MISO's alone and transfers nothing. The identification source is the same for every ISO and needs no transfer: its own vintage EIA-860 Schedule-3 planned dates, vintage-gated, reversal registry armed, the economic screen on the residual undated fleet. OPEN HERE: this ISO's own T1-H measurement of its own exit cohort (recall / total_gw / false_retire / screen displacement / adequacy response), which nothing in D42 or D44 supplies. Every pre-2026-09-03 forecast bundle of this ISO records the SUPERSEDED default-off posture and is Q30-stale — it joins the director's batched re-measure decision; D44 re-solved nothing. Backcast lane n/a and byte-identical (forecast-mode-only channel). MEASURED AT NYISO 2026-09-04 BY capx D45-R (FINDING-capx-d45-pjm-nyiso-curves-2026-09-03.md section 5.1; run nyiso-2021-2025-realized-t1h-d45r, cache key 91686abe7a744a88, bare nyiso-t1h; the FFR-3A-2 record preserved at nyiso-t1h-pre-d45r -- a CONFOUNDED comparator, a month of HEAD apart, so nothing is attributed across it). The channel holds essentially NOTHING at NYISO: the vintage-2020 EIA-860 carries 16 live rows / 512 MW in 2021-2025, 507 MW of it one 2023 gas_ct plant, and the forward set is 2 rows / 22 MW (2026-2027). Measured: gas_ct 420.3 MW retire:announced in 2023 -- the ONLY fossil exit the live NYISO T1-H produces (the economic screen decided nothing at the flat $110 anchor; the other exit is the announced nuclear 1,036 MW). It moves retire.total_gw 1.036 -> 1.457 GW against a 1.711 GW target (FAIL at -14.9 %, where the 2026-07-14 posture read -30 % against the then 1.488 target), recall 1/1 PASS, and false_retire 0.024 -> 0.256 GW (0.176, FAIL -- gas_ct 0.42 vs 0.189 actual). Verdict stays O: the cohort measurement is supplied and reads MIXED (total closer, false worse), and at NYISO the channel is a 0.4 GW input to a 1.7 GW target, not a screen-shaping mechanism -- the NYISO exit question is the flat-anchor / position artifact the D45 finding adjudicates (section 5-6), not this channel. Determination HOLD, unchanged." },
